{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-314521",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the rectangular prism, let $S$ be its surface area, and let $V$ be its volume. The variables $x,S,$ and $V$ change with time. In particular, we are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =15\\text{ in}, \\\\ z & =24\\text{ in}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =8\\text{ in}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nWe want to find the rate of change of $S$ knowing the rate of change of $x.$ So, we start with the formula for the surface area of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nS=2xz+2xy+2yz\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known values, we get\n\n$$\nS=2(x)(24)+2x(15)+2(15)(24)=78x+720.\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =78(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the above expression using $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=8,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =78(8)=624.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rectangular prism's surface area is increasing at a rate of $624\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{min}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
